<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Disclosure of LLM Usage</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLMs were used to aid and polish the writing throughout the paper. In addition, LLMs were used for retrieval and discovery to help write the Related Works section.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Other Related Works</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Extreme Bandits.</span>
Another related line of work is the <em id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">extreme bandit problem</em>, which optimizes the maximum observed reward rather than cumulative reward <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Streeter &amp; Smith, </a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cicirello &amp; Smith, </a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bhatt et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. This is closely aligned with best-of-<math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> sampling, where one selects the highest-quality output among multiple candidates. However, most extreme bandit formulations assume repeated rounds of play, while inference requires efficient decision-making in a single prompt. Our framework adapts these insights to one-shot inference with explicit cost–quality tradeoffs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cascading, Routing, and Hybrid Strategies.</span>
Beyond stopping and sampling, researchers have explored <em id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cascaded or routed inference</em> to reduce cost. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. (2024)</a></cite> escalate from cheaper to larger models only when necessary, using self-testing to decide. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mohammadshahi et al. (2024)</a></cite> learn to route prompts among multiple models, balancing cost and performance. These strategies complement our focus by showing that adaptive allocation can occur across models as well as within a single model’s sampling process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>UCB Pandora’s Box Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C UCB Pandora’s Box Algorithm ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> provides the exact pseudo-code for the algorithm outlined in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> UCB Pandora’s Box Algorithm</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg2.4" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><span id="alg2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Distribution family <math id="alg2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, sampling cost <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg2.5" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="alg2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter:</span> Confidence level parameter <math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_figure_panel ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> (set of observed sample values).

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (maximum value seen so far).

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{+}=M_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{+}=M_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (a large initial upper confidence bound for the fair cap).

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&lt;\tau^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&lt;\tau^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            Query sample and obtain <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\sim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\sim D</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow S\cup\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow S\cup\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\leftarrow\mathop{max}\{M,v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\leftarrow\mathop{max}\{M,v\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
            Update <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>: Compute the UCB for the fair-cap value <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="alg2.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math>, based on <math id="alg2.l8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the confidence parameter <math id="alg2.l8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Missing Figures</h2>

<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01394v1/frequency.png" id="A4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/137;" width="548" height="137" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>
Median rewards across <math id="A4.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="960" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>960</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">960</annotation></semantics></math> generations for <math id="A4.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> prompts from the AlpacaEval dataset.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We find that the median reward across 960 generations can vary significantly across prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Upper bound on Additive Sub-optimality). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we include all missing proofs and helper lemmas needed to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Upper bound on Additive Sub-optimality). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. The following helper lemmas will be useful.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be any distribution, <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the cost value for each sample, and <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the fair-cap value according to Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1 (Fair-cap value). ‣ 2.3 Optimal Stopping, Pandora’s Box, and Weitzman’s Algorithm ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. For every <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]\geq c-\sigma\cdot(1-F(\tau))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]\geq c-\sigma\cdot(1-F(\tau)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <em id="Thmtheorem12.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">CDF</em> of <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe the following sequence of inequalities.</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]-c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-\tau]_{+}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-\tau]_{+}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{v\sim D}\left[v\geq\tau\right]\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-\tau-\sigma]_{+}-(v-\tau)|v\geq\tau\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{v\sim D}\left[v\geq\tau\right]\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[[v-\tau-\sigma]_{+}-(v-\tau)|v\geq\tau\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}_{v\sim D}\left[v\geq\tau\right]\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[v-\tau-\sigma-(v-\tau)|v\geq\tau\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}_{v\sim D}\left[v\geq\tau\right]\mathbb{E}_{v\sim D}\left[v-\tau-\sigma-(v-\tau)|v\geq\tau\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-F(\tau))\cdot(-\sigma)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-F(\tau))\cdot(-\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be any distribution, <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the cost value for each sample and <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the fair-cap value according to Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1 (Fair-cap value). ‣ 2.3 Optimal Stopping, Pandora’s Box, and Weitzman’s Algorithm ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Then, for every <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we have that</span></p>
<table id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{v_{1:n-1}\sim D^{n-1}}\left[\mathop{max}\{v_{1},\dots,v_{n-1}\}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma]\right]\leq F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma)-F^{n-1}(\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{v_{1:n-1}\sim D^{n-1}}\left[\mathop{max}\{v_{1},\dots,v_{n-1}\}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma]\right]\leq F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma)-F^{n-1}(\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n-1}=\mathop{max}\{v_{1},\dots,v_{n-1}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n-1}=\mathop{max}\{v_{1},\dots,v_{n-1}\}.</annotation></semantics></math> Observe that <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\leq x\right]=F^{n-1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\leq x\right]=F^{n-1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the CDF of <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v_{1:n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1:n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are iid draws. Noting that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma]\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\leq\tau+\sigma\right]-\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\leq\tau\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma]\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\leq\tau+\sigma\right]-\mathbb{P}\left[M_{n-1}\leq\tau\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be any distribution, <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the cost value for each sample, and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the fair-cap value according to Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1 (Fair-cap value). ‣ 2.3 Optimal Stopping, Pandora’s Box, and Weitzman’s Algorithm ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Then, for every <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{v_{1:n}\sim D^{n}}\left[\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]\geq-\sigma(1-F(\tau))\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{v_{1:n}\sim D^{n}}\left[\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]\geq-\sigma(1-F(\tau))\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{n}:=[v_{n}-\mathop{max}\{v_{1:n-1}\}]_{+}-c," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{n}:=[v_{n}-\mathop{max}\{v_{1:n-1}\}]_{+}-c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the event that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{max}\{v_{1:n-1}\}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{max}\{v_{1:n-1}\}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">(of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem14" title="Lemma 14. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>)
It suffices to prove the lower bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta_{n}|v_{1:n-1}\right]\geq-\sigma(1-F(\tau))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta_{n}|v_{1:n-1}\right]\geq-\sigma(1-F(\tau))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">on the event that <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs. Since <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v_{1:n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1:n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta_{n}|v_{1:n-1}\right]\geq\mathbb{E}\left[[v_{n}-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]-c\geq-\sigma\cdot(1-F(\tau))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\Delta_{n}|v_{1:n-1}\right]\geq\mathbb{E}\left[[v_{n}-(\tau+\sigma)]_{+}\right]-c\geq-\sigma\cdot(1-F(\tau)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We are now ready to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Upper bound on Additive Sub-optimality). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Upper bound on Additive Sub-optimality). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) Let <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the sampling cost and <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> be any family of distributions that admits an anytime-valid upper confidence bound <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau^{+}_{\delta}(n,v_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{+}_{\delta}(n,v_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math> with width function <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix some <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the iid sequence <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2}\dots\sim D." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2}\dots\sim D.</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the fair-cap value of <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> denote the CDF of <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D.</annotation></semantics></math> For every <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event in Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 4 (Anytime Valid Upper Confidence Bound on the Fair-cap Value). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{n-1}=\mathop{max}\{v_{1:n-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n-1}=\mathop{max}\{v_{1:n-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{n}:=[v_{n}-M_{n-1}]_{+}-c" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{n}:=[v_{n}-M_{n-1}]_{+}-c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{n}:=\{M_{n-1}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)]\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}:=\{M_{n-1}\in[\tau,\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)]\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">On the event <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two policies disagree only when event <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left((R_{W}-R_{U})\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left((R_{W}-R_{U})\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to use Fubini’s theorem to swap the expectation with the sum. To do so, we need to show that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[|-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}|\right]&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[|-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}|\right]&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">To see this, note that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}|\leq(c+[v_{n}-M_{n-1}]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\leq(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}|\leq(c+[v_{n}-M_{n-1}]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\leq(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from the fact that on <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n-1}\geq\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n-1}\geq\tau.</annotation></semantics></math> Thus, it suffices to upper bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">By conditioning on <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and using the tower law, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}|M_{n-1}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[(c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+})\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}|M_{n-1}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+}|M_{n-1}\right]\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+}|M_{n-1}\right]\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+}\right]\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[c+[v_{n}-\tau]_{+}\right]\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[2c\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[2c\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2c\cdot\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2c\cdot\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2c\cdot\left(F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F^{n-1}(\tau)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2c\cdot\left(F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F^{n-1}(\tau)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2c\cdot F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2c\cdot F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">where the third equality is by independence of <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fourth equality is by definition of <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, and the sixth equality by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[|-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}|\right]\leq 2c\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))&lt;\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[|-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}|\right]\leq 2c\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))&lt;\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\rightarrow\infty." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\rightarrow\infty.</annotation></semantics></math> Accordingly, by Fubini’s, theorem, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left((R_{W}-R_{U})\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left((R_{W}-R_{U})\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem14" title="Lemma 14. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)(1-F(\tau))\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[-\Delta_{n}\mathbf{1}_{B_{n}}\mathbf{1}_{E_{\delta}}\right]\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)(1-F(\tau))\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.11.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]=F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F^{n-1}(\tau)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[B_{n}\right]=F^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F^{n-1}(\tau),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.12.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 7 (Sub-optimality gap upper bound for Exponential distribution). ‣ 3.2 Example: Exponential distribution with unknown parameter 𝜆 ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we include all missing proofs and helper lemmas needed to prove Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 7 (Sub-optimality gap upper bound for Exponential distribution). ‣ 3.2 Example: Exponential distribution with unknown parameter 𝜆 ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to use Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Upper bound on Additive Sub-optimality). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we need to specify several things. First, Lemma<a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 15 (Fair-cap value for Exponential distribution). ‣ E.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> computes the fair cap value for an Exponential distribution with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fair-cap value for Exponential distribution)<span id="Thmtheorem15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be the exponential distribution with parameter <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math> Then, for every <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the fair cap value <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> associated with <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{\lambda c}\right)}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{\lambda c}\right)}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\sim\operatorname{Exp}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\sim\operatorname{Exp}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[[v-\tau]_{+}\right]=\int_{\tau}^{\infty}(x-\tau)\lambda e^{-\lambda x}=\frac{e^{-\lambda\tau}}{\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[[v-\tau]_{+}\right]=\int_{\tau}^{\infty}(x-\tau)\lambda e^{-\lambda x}=\frac{e^{-\lambda\tau}}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Setting this equal to <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we need to derive an anytime valid upper confidence bound on the fair-cap value for the Exponential distribution with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math> Note that an upper confidence bound on <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> gives an upper confidence bound on <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is an exponential distribution with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, as a first step, Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16 (Anytime-valid Confidence Sequence for Exponential distribution). ‣ E.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> derives an anytime-valid confidence sequence for the mean of the Exponential distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Anytime-valid Confidence Sequence for Exponential distribution)<span id="Thmtheorem16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be an Exponential distribution with parameter <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math> Define</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{\delta}(n):=\mathop{min}\Biggl\{\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\frac{6}{n}\log\left(\frac{2n(n+1)}{\delta}\right)}\Biggl\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\delta}(n):=\mathop{min}\Biggl\{\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\frac{6}{n}\log\left(\frac{2n(n+1)}{\delta}\right)}\Biggl\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for every <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{v_{1:\infty}\sim D^{\infty}}\left[\forall n\geq 1:\mu\in[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))]\right]\geq 1-\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{v_{1:\infty}\sim D^{\infty}}\left[\forall n\geq 1:\mu\in[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))]\right]\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{n}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}v_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{n}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}v_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be an exponential distribution with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math> Let <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2},\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2},\dots</annotation></semantics></math> denote a sequence of iid draws from <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math> Define <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=v_{i}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=v_{i}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1/\lambda." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1/\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math> Note that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\sim\operatorname{Exp}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\sim\operatorname{Exp}(1).</annotation></semantics></math> Fix some <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}\sim\operatorname{Gamma}(n,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Gamma</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}\sim\operatorname{Gamma}(n,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}=\frac{S_{n}}{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}=\frac{S_{n}}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math> For any <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> we will show that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\geq\frac{1}{1-s}\right]\leq e^{-n\psi_{+}(s)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\geq\frac{1}{1-s}\right]\leq e^{-n\psi_{+}(s)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\leq\frac{1}{1+s}\right]\leq e^{-n\psi_{-}(s)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\leq\frac{1}{1+s}\right]\leq e^{-n\psi_{-}(s)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{+}(s):=\frac{s}{1-s}+\log(1-s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{+}(s):=\frac{s}{1-s}+\log(1-s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{-}(s):=\log(1+s)-\frac{s}{1+s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{-}(s):=\log(1+s)-\frac{s}{1+s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Starting with the upper tail, by Markov’s inequality and the MGF of the <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Gamma}(n,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Gamma</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Gamma}(n,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[S_{n}\geq a\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[e^{sS_{n}}\geq e^{sa}\right]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[e^{sS_{n}}\right]}{e^{sa}}=(1-s)^{-n}e^{-sa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[S_{n}\geq a\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[e^{sS_{n}}\geq e^{sa}\right]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[e^{sS_{n}}\right]}{e^{sa}}=(1-s)^{-n}e^{-sa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">With <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\frac{n}{1-s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\frac{n}{1-s}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\geq\frac{1}{1-s}\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[S_{n}\geq a\right]\leq\exp\left(-n\left(\frac{s}{1-s}+\log(1-s)\right)\right)=e^{-n\psi_{+}(s)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\geq\frac{1}{1-s}\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[S_{n}\geq a\right]\leq\exp\left(-n\left(\frac{s}{1-s}+\log(1-s)\right)\right)=e^{-n\psi_{+}(s)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">For the lower tail, we use the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\rightarrow e^{-sx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\rightarrow e^{-sx}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing to get that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[S_{n}\leq a\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[e^{-sS_{n}}\geq e^{-sa}\right]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[e^{-sS_{n}}\right]}{e^{-sa}}=(1+s)^{-n}e^{sa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[S_{n}\leq a\right]=\mathbb{P}\left[e^{-sS_{n}}\geq e^{-sa}\right]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[e^{-sS_{n}}\right]}{e^{-sa}}=(1+s)^{-n}e^{sa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\frac{n}{1+s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\frac{n}{1+s}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\leq\frac{1}{1+s}\right]\leq e^{-n\psi_{-}(s)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}}{\mu}\leq\frac{1}{1+s}\right]\leq e^{-n\psi_{-}(s)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we show that for any <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{+}(s)\geq\frac{s^{2}}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{+}(s)\geq\frac{s^{2}}{6}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{-}(s)\geq\frac{s^{2}}{6}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{-}(s)\geq\frac{s^{2}}{6}.</annotation></semantics></math> For <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{+}(s)=\psi_{+}(s)-s^{2}/6." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{+}(s)=\psi_{+}(s)-s^{2}/6.</annotation></semantics></math> Then, note that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}_{+}(s)=\frac{s}{(1-s)^{2}}-\frac{s}{3}=s\left(\frac{1}{(1-s)^{2}}-\frac{1}{3}\right)\geq\frac{2s}{3}\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}_{+}(s)=\frac{s}{(1-s)^{2}}-\frac{s}{3}=s\left(\frac{1}{(1-s)^{2}}-\frac{1}{3}\right)\geq\frac{2s}{3}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{+}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{+}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}_{+}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}_{+}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> we have that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{+}(s)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{+}(s)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math>
For <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{-}(s)=\log(1+s)-\frac{s}{1+s}\geq\left(s-\frac{s^{2}}{2}\right)-\left(s-\frac{s^{2}}{1+s}\right)=s^{2}\left(\frac{1}{1+s}-\frac{1}{2}\right)=\frac{s^{2}(1-s)}{2(1+s)}\geq\frac{s^{2}}{6}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{-}(s)=\log(1+s)-\frac{s}{1+s}\geq\left(s-\frac{s^{2}}{2}\right)-\left(s-\frac{s^{2}}{1+s}\right)=s^{2}\left(\frac{1}{1+s}-\frac{1}{2}\right)=\frac{s^{2}(1-s)}{2(1+s)}\geq\frac{s^{2}}{6},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.11.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality is due to the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+s)\geq s-\frac{s^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+s)\geq s-\frac{s^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and the last inequality uses the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq 1/2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq 1/2.</annotation></semantics></math> We now complete the proof by picking a summable sequence <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math> Namely, pick <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{n}=\frac{\delta}{n(n+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{n}=\frac{\delta}{n(n+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and note that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n\geq 1}\delta_{n}=\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n\geq 1}\delta_{n}=\delta.</annotation></semantics></math> At time <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, pick</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{\delta}(n):=\mathop{min}\Biggl\{\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\frac{6}{n}\log\left(\frac{2}{\delta_{n}}\right)}\Biggl\}=\mathop{min}\Biggl\{\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\frac{6}{n}\log\left(\frac{2n(n+1)}{\delta}\right)}\Biggl\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\delta}(n):=\mathop{min}\Biggl\{\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\frac{6}{n}\log\left(\frac{2}{\delta_{n}}\right)}\Biggl\}=\mathop{min}\Biggl\{\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\frac{6}{n}\log\left(\frac{2n(n+1)}{\delta}\right)}\Biggl\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.12.1" class="ltx_text">Our previous analysis, then gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\mu\notin[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))]\right]\leq\delta_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\mu\notin[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))]\right]\leq\delta_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.13.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, by the union bound, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\exists n\geq 1:\mu\notin[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))]\right]\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\delta_{n}=\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\exists n\geq 1:\mu\notin[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))]\right]\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\delta_{n}=\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.14.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the anytime-valid upper confidence bound on the mean <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> given by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16 (Anytime-valid Confidence Sequence for Exponential distribution). ‣ E.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> can be computed just from the observed rewards. Hence, it applies to <em id="A5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> distribution in our distribution family <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}.</annotation></semantics></math> With Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16 (Anytime-valid Confidence Sequence for Exponential distribution). ‣ E.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> in hand, we can now prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Anytime-valid Upper Confidence Bound for Exponential Fair-cap value). ‣ 3.2 Example: Exponential distribution with unknown parameter 𝜆 ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, which gives an anytime-valid upper confidence bound on the fair-cap value for the family of Exponential distributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Anytime-valid Upper Confidence Bound for Exponential Fair-cap value). ‣ 3.2 Example: Exponential distribution with unknown parameter 𝜆 ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) Let <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the sampling cost and <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> be the class of Exponential distribution with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in(0,\frac{1}{c\cdot e}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in(0,\frac{1}{c\cdot e}].</annotation></semantics></math> Fix a distribution <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}\in\mathcal{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}\in\mathcal{F}.</annotation></semantics></math> Let <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the fair-cap value and <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be the mean of <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, let <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the iid sequence <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2},\dots\sim D_{\lambda}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2},\dots\sim D_{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16 (Anytime-valid Confidence Sequence for Exponential distribution). ‣ E.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\forall n\geq 1:\mu\in[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\right]\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\forall n\geq 1:\mu\in[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\right]\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma<a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 15 (Fair-cap value for Exponential distribution). ‣ E.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix E Missing Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we know that for the exponential distribution, its cap value is a monotonic in <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, with probability <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\forall n\geq 1:\tau\in\left[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)\right]\right]\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\forall n\geq 1:\tau\in\left[\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right),\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)\right]\right]\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau^{+}_{\delta}(n,v_{1:n}):=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{+}_{\delta}(n,v_{1:n}):=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right).</annotation></semantics></math> To complete the proof, it suffices to upper bound the difference</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)-\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)-\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the function <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\mu)=\mu\log(\mu/c)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\mu)=\mu\log(\mu/c).</annotation></semantics></math> Then, by the Mean Value Theorem and the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(\mu)=1+\log\left(\frac{\mu}{c}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(\mu)=1+\log\left(\frac{\mu}{c}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g(\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n)))-g(\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n)))-g(\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1-r_{\delta}(n)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)\right)(2\widehat{\mu}_{n}r_{\delta}(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)\right)(2\widehat{\mu}_{n}r_{\delta}(n))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)\right)\left(\frac{2r_{\delta}(n)\mu}{1-r_{\delta}(n)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{n}(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c}\right)\right)\left(\frac{2r_{\delta}(n)\mu}{1-r_{\delta}(n)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\mu(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c(1-r_{\delta}(n))}\right)\right)\left(\frac{2r_{\delta}(n)\mu}{1-r_{\delta}(n)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\mu(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c(1-r_{\delta}(n))}\right)\right)\left(\frac{2r_{\delta}(n)\mu}{1-r_{\delta}(n)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\delta}(n)\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\delta}(n)\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by definition. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\mu(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c(1-r_{\delta}(n))}\right)\right)\left(\frac{2r_{\delta}(n)\mu}{1-r_{\delta}(n)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(1+\log\left(\frac{\mu(1+r_{\delta}(n))}{c(1-r_{\delta}(n))}\right)\right)\left(\frac{2r_{\delta}(n)\mu}{1-r_{\delta}(n)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(3+\log\left(\frac{\mu}{c}\right)\right)\left(4r_{\delta}(n)\mu\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(3+\log\left(\frac{\mu}{c}\right)\right)\left(4r_{\delta}(n)\mu\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4r_{\delta}(n)\cdot\tau\cdot\left(1+\frac{3}{\log\left(\frac{\mu}{c}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4r_{\delta}(n)\cdot\tau\cdot\left(1+\frac{3}{\log\left(\frac{\mu}{c}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 16r_{\delta}(n)\cdot\tau," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 16r_{\delta}(n)\cdot\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from the assumption that <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\geq e\cdot c." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\geq e\cdot c.</annotation></semantics></math> Hence, altogether, we can take</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)=16r_{\delta}(n)\cdot\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)=16r_{\delta}(n)\cdot\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we use Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Upper bound on Additive Sub-optimality). ‣ 3.1 Main Theoretical Result ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> to bound the sub-optimality gap for UCB Pandora’s Box algorithm for the family <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> of Exponential distributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">(of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 7 (Sub-optimality gap upper bound for Exponential distribution). ‣ 3.2 Example: Exponential distribution with unknown parameter 𝜆 ‣ 3 Pandora’s Box with Unknown Reward Distributions ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) Let <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> be the class of Exponential distribution with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in(0,\frac{1}{c\cdot e}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in(0,\frac{1}{c\cdot e}].</annotation></semantics></math> Fix a distribution <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}\in\mathcal{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}\in\mathcal{F}.</annotation></semantics></math> Let <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau(D,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau(D,c)</annotation></semantics></math> be the fair-cap value and let <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)(1-F_{\lambda}(\tau))\cdot(F^{n-1}_{\lambda}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F_{\lambda}^{n-1}(\tau))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)(1-F_{\lambda}(\tau))\cdot(F^{n-1}_{\lambda}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F_{\lambda}^{n-1}(\tau))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the Mean Value Theorem and the fact that the PDF <math id="A5.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically decreasing, we have that for some <math id="A5.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in(\tau,\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in(\tau,\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{\lambda}^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F_{\lambda}^{n-1}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{\lambda}^{n-1}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))-F_{\lambda}^{n-1}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(b)\cdot f_{\lambda}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(b)\cdot f_{\lambda}(b)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))\cdot f_{\lambda}(\tau)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))\cdot f_{\lambda}(\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging this back in gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(1-F_{\lambda}(\tau))\cdot\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))\cdot f(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(1-F_{\lambda}(\tau))\cdot\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))\cdot f(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)^{2}\cdot(1-F_{\lambda}(\tau))\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))\cdot f_{\lambda}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n)^{2}\cdot(1-F_{\lambda}(\tau))\cdot(n-1)\cdot F_{\lambda}^{n-2}(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))\cdot f_{\lambda}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}256\cdot\tau^{2}r_{\delta}(n)^{2}\cdot e^{-\lambda\tau}\cdot(n-1)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))})^{n-2}\cdot\lambda\cdot e^{-\lambda\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}256\cdot\tau^{2}r_{\delta}(n)^{2}\cdot e^{-\lambda\tau}\cdot(n-1)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+\sigma_{\delta,\tau}(n))})^{n-2}\cdot\lambda\cdot e^{-\lambda\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now, observe that <math id="A5.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\delta}(n)^{2}\leq C\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\delta}(n)^{2}\leq C\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for some universal constant <math id="A5.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leq\frac{256\cdot C\tau^{2}\lambda}{e^{2\lambda\tau}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leq\frac{256\cdot C\tau^{2}\lambda}{e^{2\lambda\tau}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to upper bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=e^{-\lambda\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=e^{-\lambda\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{n}:=1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n}:=1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))}.</annotation></semantics></math> Then, observe that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{n}=1-Ae^{-16\lambda\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>λ</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n}=1-Ae^{-16\lambda\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">We want to find the smallest <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\lambda\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n)\leq\log 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\lambda\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n)\leq\log 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the definition of <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\delta}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\delta}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> gives that we need to set</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq\Theta\left(\lambda^{2}\tau^{2}\log(1/\delta)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq\Theta\left(\lambda^{2}\tau^{2}\log(1/\delta)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">For this choice of <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for all <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-16\lambda\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n)}\geq\frac{1}{2}\implies q_{n}\leq 1-\frac{A}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>λ</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-16\lambda\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n)}\geq\frac{1}{2}\implies q_{n}\leq 1-\frac{A}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for all <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{n-2}_{n}\leq\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{n-2}_{n}\leq\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.6.1" class="ltx_text">Now, split the infinite sum</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}=\sum_{n&lt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}+\sum_{n&gt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}=\sum_{n&lt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}+\sum_{n&gt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.7.1" class="ltx_text">We can trivially bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n&lt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}\leq N\log(N/\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n&lt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}\leq N\log(N/\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.8.1" class="ltx_text">As for the second sum, we claim that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n&gt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}\leq O\left(\frac{\log(2/\delta A)}{A}\right)=O\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\cdot\log(1/\delta)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n&gt;N}\log(n/\delta)\cdot q_{n}^{n-2}\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}\leq O\left(\frac{\log(2/\delta A)}{A}\right)=O\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\cdot\log(1/\delta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.9.1" class="ltx_text">To see why the second inequality is true, let <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:=1-\frac{A}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:=1-\frac{A}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math> Then,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}=\frac{1}{q^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}=\frac{1}{q^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.10.1" class="ltx_text">We will focus on bounding <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math> Define <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}=(1-q)q^{n-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}=(1-q)q^{n-1}.</annotation></semantics></math> Note that <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the PMF of a geometric distribution <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-q</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}=\frac{q}{1-q}\sum_{n\geq 1}p_{n}\log(n/\delta)=\frac{q}{1-q}\mathbb{E}_{n\sim p}\left[\log(n/\delta)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}=\frac{q}{1-q}\sum_{n\geq 1}p_{n}\log(n/\delta)=\frac{q}{1-q}\mathbb{E}_{n\sim p}\left[\log(n/\delta)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.11.1" class="ltx_text">By Jensen’s inequality and the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(x/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(x/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> is concave, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{n\sim p}\left[\log(n/\delta)\right]\leq\log\left(\mathbb{E}_{n\sim p}\left[n/\delta\right]\right)=\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{n\sim p}\left[\log(n/\delta)\right]\leq\log\left(\mathbb{E}_{n\sim p}\left[n/\delta\right]\right)=\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.12.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}\leq\frac{q}{1-q}\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}\leq\frac{q}{1-q}\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.13.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{q^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}\leq\frac{1}{q(1-q)}\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{q^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}\leq\frac{1}{q(1-q)}\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.14.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{q^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}\leq\frac{2}{(1-q)}\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{q^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)q^{n}\leq\frac{2}{(1-q)}\log\left(\frac{1}{\delta(1-q)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.15.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging in <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=1-\frac{A}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=1-\frac{A}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> completes the claim that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}\leq O\left(\frac{\log(2/\delta A)}{A}\right)=O\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\cdot\log(1/\delta)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\left(1-\frac{A}{2}\right)^{n-2}\leq O\left(\frac{\log(2/\delta A)}{A}\right)=O\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\cdot\log(1/\delta)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.16.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equality follows from the definition of <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A.</annotation></semantics></math> Now, returning to the original proof, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}\leq\widetilde{O}_{\delta,\tau,\lambda}(\lambda^{2}\tau^{2})+\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\log(n/\delta)\cdot(1-e^{-\lambda(\tau+16\tau\cdot r_{\delta}(n))})^{n-2}\leq\widetilde{O}_{\delta,\tau,\lambda}(\lambda^{2}\tau^{2})+\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.17.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying by the outer factor gives that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{256\cdot C\tau^{2}\lambda}{e^{2\lambda\tau}}\left(\widetilde{O}_{\delta,\tau,\lambda}(\lambda^{2}\tau^{2})+O\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{256\cdot C\tau^{2}\lambda}{e^{2\lambda\tau}}\left(\widetilde{O}_{\delta,\tau,\lambda}(\lambda^{2}\tau^{2})+O\left(\lambda\tau\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{\lambda^{3}\tau^{4}}{e^{2\lambda\tau}}+\frac{\lambda^{2}\tau^{3}}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{\lambda^{3}\tau^{4}}{e^{2\lambda\tau}}+\frac{\lambda^{2}\tau^{3}}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\tau^{3}}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\left(1+\frac{\lambda\tau}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\tau^{3}}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\left(1+\frac{\lambda\tau}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\tau^{3}}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\tau^{3}}{e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{(\lambda\tau)^{3}}{\lambda\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{(\lambda\tau)^{3}}{\lambda\cdot e^{\lambda\tau}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{1}{\lambda}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{O}_{\delta}\left(\frac{1}{\lambda}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p12.18.1" class="ltx_text">The third fifth equality follows from the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{x}{e^{x}}=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{x}{e^{x}}=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{x^{4}}{e^{x}}=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{x^{4}}{e^{x}}=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides comprehensive experimental results across all datasets, language models, and reward models. While Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Experimental Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> focused on representative examples, here we present the complete evaluation demonstrating the consistency and robustness of our adaptive approach.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Experiment 1: Profit Performance Across All Configurations</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate how consistently our adaptive algorithm matches optimal non-adaptive performance across diverse settings. The profit performance ratio is defined as:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Profit Performance Ratio}=\frac{\text{Profit of Adaptive Best-of-N}}{\text{Profit of Best Non-adaptive Best-of-N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Profit Performance Ratio</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>Profit of Adaptive Best-of-N</mtext><mtext>Profit of Best Non-adaptive Best-of-N</mtext></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Profit Performance Ratio}=\frac{\text{Profit of Adaptive Best-of-N}}{\text{Profit of Best Non-adaptive Best-of-N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where profit equals utility minus total generation cost. A ratio near 1.0 indicates the adaptive algorithm matches the best possible non-adaptive strategy without requiring hyperparameter tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results, shown in Figure <a href="#A6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ F.1 Experiment 1: Profit Performance Across All Configurations ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for the AlpacaFarm and HH-RLHF datasets with RM-Mistral-7B and FsfairX-LLaMA3-RM-v0.1, confirm the adaptive algorithm’s strength.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The adaptive algorithm outperforms most of the time even the best-tuned generator dependent non-adaptive strategy. This implies that its dynamic behavior is more profitable than any fixed, one-size-fits-all approach.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/cost_alpaca_mistral.png" id="A6.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/135;" width="548" height="135" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/cost_alpaca_fsfair.png" id="A6.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/135;" width="548" height="135" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/cost_rlhf_mistral.png" id="A6.F5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/135;" width="548" height="135" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/cost_rlhf_fsfair.png" id="A6.F5.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/135;" width="548" height="135" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Profit performance ratios for four LLM generators across varying cost/utility ratios. Each panel represents a different dataset-reward model combination, with four cost/utility scenarios per panel. Higher ratios indicate better profit efficiency relative to best non-adaptive algorithm.

</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Experiment 2: Win Rate Analysis Across Configurations</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare head-to-head performance when adaptive and non-adaptive algorithms use identical computation budgets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/win_rate_alpaca_mistral.png" id="A6.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/184;" width="494" height="184" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/win_rate_alpaca_fsfair.png" id="A6.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/184;" width="494" height="184" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/win_rate_rlhf_mistral.png" id="A6.F6.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/184;" width="494" height="184" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/win_rate_rlhf_fsfair.png" id="A6.F6.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/184;" width="494" height="184" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>
Performance evaluation of adaptive versus non-adaptive generation under matched computational budgets. Each row corresponds to a unique reward model-dataset configuration. Left panels present win rates computed from 100 sample permutations where adaptive algorithms compete against non-adaptive baselines. Right panels show mean sample counts (identical for both strategies due to budget matching) averaged over the same 100 permutations. Both metrics are plotted against cost (log scale, <math id="A6.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and represent median values across all evaluation prompts.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ F.2 Experiment 2: Win Rate Analysis Across Configurations ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reveals consistent patterns across all settings:</p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Budget scaling:</span> The adaptive algorithm’s advantage grows with the available budget. Its win rate increases from around 50% (at chance) with minimal resources to over 54% when the budget exceeds 100 samples.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model consistency:</span> The win rate trends are remarkably consistent across different models. This demonstrates that the algorithm’s effectiveness is not tied to a specific model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset effects:</span> Similarly, the performance curves hold steady across different datasets, proving the algorithm is robust to variations in input data and prompt styles.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This consistent advantage across diverse models, datasets, and budgets validates our central hypothesis: the adaptive algorithm succeeds by exploiting the unique reward distribution of each prompt, rather than relying on a specific setup.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Experiment 3: Efficiency Gains at Target Quality Levels</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This experiment quantifies the computational efficiency of our adaptive algorithm. We measure how many fewer samples it needs than a non-adaptive approach to reach the same quality, defined by the acceptance rate.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/save_ratio_alpaca_mistral.png" id="A6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/186;" width="494" height="186" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/save_ratio_alpaca_fsfair.png" id="A6.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/186;" width="494" height="186" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/save_ratio_rlhf_mistral.png" id="A6.F7.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/186;" width="494" height="186" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.01394v1/save_ratio_rlhf_fsfair.png" id="A6.F7.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/186;" width="494" height="186" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Computational savings from adaptive generation while maintaining acceptance rate equivalence. Each row presents a unique reward model-dataset pairing. Left panels quantify the save ratio—the fraction of samples eliminated by adaptive algorithms compared to non-adaptive methods when both achieve identical average acceptance rates. Specifically, for each target acceptance rate, the adaptive algorithm yields an actual acceptance rate, and the non-adaptive sample count is calibrated to match this actual rate. Right panels show the relationship between target and actual acceptance rates for the adaptive algorithm, illustrating calibration behavior. Save ratios are averaged over 100 generation stream permutations, with all metrics indexed by target acceptance rate (0.6–1.0) and aggregated via median across 100 test prompts.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ F.3 Experiment 3: Efficiency Gains at Target Quality Levels ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Optimal Stopping vs Best-Of-𝑁for Inference Time Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> demonstrates two critical findings:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right panels (Target vs Achieved Rates):</span> The adaptive algorithm effectively follows the desired quality targets. While a small gap exists between the target and achieved acceptance rates, the graphs confirm that our algorithm reliably adjusts its behavior to closely approximate the specified quality level across all configurations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left panels (Compute Savings):</span> The algorithm delivers significant efficiency gains, with savings that peak when targeting high levels of quality. The trend is as follows:</p>
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Savings increase from 10% at a moderate quality target (0.70 acceptance rate) to a peak of <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 30</annotation></semantics></math>% for near-optimal targets (0.90+ acceptance rate).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">However, savings decrease as the target approaches 100%. This is because the extreme quality requirement forces the adaptive algorithm to use its maximum sample budget, causing its behavior to converge with the non-adaptive baseline. Importantly, even in this scenario, it never performs worse.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This peak in savings at high (but not perfect) quality levels demonstrates the algorithm’s core strength: its ability to recognize when a near-optimal response has been found and stop generation early. In contrast, non-adaptive methods must always continue sampling to maintain the same quality guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Efficiency gains increase monotonically with target quality:</p>
<ul id="A6.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Roughly 10% savings at 0.70 acceptance rate (moderate quality)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Roughly 20% savings at 0.80 acceptance rate (good quality)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Roughly 30% savings at 0.90+ acceptance rate (near-optimal quality)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When 100% acceptance rate is targeted, our experimental setup suffers from maximum sample size leading that adaptive algorithm becomes closer to non-adaptive one. This explains decrease on save ratio as we get close to 100% target acceptance rate though it never performs worse than non-adaptive algorithm with same computation budget.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The increasing savings at higher quality levels reflect the adaptive algorithm’s ability to recognize when it has likely found a near-optimal response, while non-adaptive methods must continue sampling to maintain guarantees.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4 </span>Cross-Dataset and Cross-Model Insights</h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A cross-experimental analysis of our results reveals three consistent and noteworthy findings:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness Across Configurations:</span> The performance metrics and advantages of the adaptive algorithm remained consistent across all 1,600 unique generation profiles. This demonstrates that the approach generalizes effectively and is not over-fit to specific model-dataset pairings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Positive Scaling with Budget:</span> The superiority of the prompt-adaptive algorithm becomes more pronounced as the number of candidate generations increases, indicating that its advantages scale positively with a larger computational budget.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Model Independence:</span> The performance trends were congruent for both the RM-Mistral-7B and FsfairX-LLaMA3-RM-v0.1 reward models. This suggests that the benefits of the adaptive strategy are independent of the specific reward function employed.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
